From 3a0d220f69a97341382b95fafa2c187c50adf880 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 04:15:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] MFront: generic integration drivers work on copies of the
 behaviour data

The drivers of the generic interface (integration, initialize functions
and post-processings of the small strain, standard finite strain,
Green-Lagrange and logarithmic strain behaviours) temporarily modified
the pointers of the behaviour data given by the caller, and restored them
afterwards. They now build a local copy of the behaviour data whose
pointers refer to the local values (Cauchy stress, Green-Lagrange strain,
etc.), and never modify the data of the caller. For the Cauchy stress,
the standard finite strain drivers directly call the small strain ones.
The results are unchanged.

With nvc++ -mp=gpu at -O2, the stress written by the initialize function
of a finite strain behaviour was lost when the fields were stored point
by point: the save and restore of the pointers around the call led to
wrong device code. The same construct was the trigger of the defect of
nvcc 13.0 worked around in PointView.
---
 .../GreenLagrangeStrainIntegrate.hxx          |  61 +++------
 .../MFront/GenericBehaviour/Integrate.hxx     |  50 +++-----
 .../LogarithmicStrainIntegrate.hxx            |  61 +++------
 ...StandardFiniteStrainBehaviourIntegrate.hxx | 118 +++++++++---------
 4 files changed, 116 insertions(+), 174 deletions(-)

